  "codebook": {
    "definition": "Credit-claiming occurs when a senator explicitly attributes a positive outcome, action, or achievement to their own efforts, advocacy, or legislative work, thereby taking personal or institutional responsibility for the result.",
    "clarification": "Credit-claiming is identified when a senator uses language such as 'I secured,' 'I helped,' 'I authored,' 'I fought for,' or similar phrases that directly link their actions to a tangible or intangible benefit. This includes securing funding, passing legislation, advocating for a cause, or achieving a policy goal. The focus is on the senator's explicit assertion of their role in bringing about the outcome.",
