        "explanation": "Senator Durbin explicitly claims credit for helping secure an expedited environmental review and federal funding for the South Suburban Airport, as well as facilitating its return to the national priority list for federal funding."
      }
    ],
    "negative_clarification": "Credit-claiming does NOT occur when a senator merely discusses, critiques, or supports an issue, policy, or outcome without explicitly linking their own actions to the result. General statements of support, criticism, or advocacy without a direct claim of responsibility do not qualify. Additionally, commemorative or honorary statements (e.g., honoring individuals or events) are not credit-claiming unless the senator explicitly ties their own efforts to the honor or commemoration.",
